\newlabel{fig:cross_campaign_lambdaW}{{17}{13}{Cross-campaign $\lambda /W$ comparison in simulation units. Longitudinal-field (blue): strong $\beta $-dependence from ${\sim }4.7$ ($\beta =0.3$) to ${\sim }2.8$ ($\beta =2.0$). Perpendicular-field (red): $\lambda /W \approx 1.25$ ($\beta \geq 1.0$) or flat profile ($\beta \leq 0.5$). Horizontal dashed line = full-sample HGBS mean ($\lambda /W_{\rm fil} = 2.79 \pm 0.09$; multiply $\lambda /W_{\rm core}$ by T1$=0.606$ or T1$=0.707$ to compare directly in observable units)}{figure.17}{}}
